*Read: GET /article/\{id\}

  A read is a producer followed by a responder.

%{snippet|file=${project.build.directory}/site-snippets/article/id.GET.yml}

  <<<LoadArticle>>> fetches the row or throws <<<NotFoundException>>>.  It publishes the entity as a
  variable.

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/scratchopenapi/LoadArticle.java}

  <<<RespondWithArticle>>> reads that entity with <<<@Val>>> and maps it to the response DTO.

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/scratchopenapi/RespondWithArticle.java}

  The two functions never reference each other.  <<<LoadArticle>>> publishes an <<<Article>>>.
  <<<RespondWithArticle>>> consumes an <<<Article>>>.  The variable type is the contract between them.


*Not found: office-level escalation

  <<<LoadArticle>>> simply throws.  A handler registered under <<<officefloor/escalation/>>> maps the
  exception to a 404.  This applies to every endpoint that loads.  There is no per-endpoint error wiring.

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/net.officefloor.tutorial.scratchopenapi.NotFoundException.yml}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/scratchopenapi/NotFoundExceptionHandler.java}


